# `specs/indexes/**` is generated by `tools/indexer.ts` and committed, so two
# branches that both touched the graph will both have regenerated it. `-merge`
# is git's binary policy: it refuses a line-level three-way merge and leaves the
# conflict standing. That is deliberate. A line merge of two regenerated indexes
# produces a file that is textually clean and semantically false, and `union` is
# worse — it emits duplicate YAML keys. Resolve by regenerating and committing
# the result: `pnpm spec:index` (here: `node_modules/.bin/tsx tools/spec.ts
# index`). Never hand-merge these files.
specs/indexes/** -merge
